(v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14885, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LzAJ3YPy5h2F3Yh5BAapQY", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14885, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LzAJ3YPy5h2F3Yh5BAapQY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17783, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident INC-0001 (SEV2):** It says v2.3.1 failed health checks, that I rolled back to v2.3.0, and what the service looks like now. It also says the next step is to find out why v2.3.1 failed before anyone redeploys it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DCWVvMbo7GbeQ31fxxT9qo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012m9euun5UTCU4fEghSJfke", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "